Workload breakdown — 3 pods, cluster-wide
 BUCKET                PODS   CPU REQ   CPU USE   MEM REQ   MEM USE   DISK REQ   DISK USE 
 platform              1      100m      3m        128Mi     20Mi      0          —        
 integrated services   1      250m      3m        512Mi     20Mi      0          —        
 applications          1      50m       3m        64Mi      20Mi      0          —        
 other                 0      0m        0m        0         0         0          —        
 TOTAL                 3      400m      9m        704Mi     60Mi      0          —        

SCHEDULABLE is allocatable − requested: what a new pod could still ask for.
FREE is allocatable − in-use: what is unused right now. A node can be fully requested
and barely used, or barely requested and full; these two columns are what tells them apart.

Disk IN-USE / FREE and the DISK USE column read `—` because the kubelet Summary API
(`/api/v1/nodes/<node>/proxy/stats/summary`) could not be read. It answered:
  solo-1: kubectl failed without a message
Disk CAPACITY, ALLOCATABLE and REQUESTED are the node's `ephemeral-storage` and are unaffected.
